-prometheus (3.5.3+ds1-1) experimental; urgency=medium
+prometheus (3.0.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium
 
-  * The Prometheus Web UI has been completely disabled in this package.
-    Upstream removed the Classic UI in v2.34.0. The newer React and Mantine
-    UIs cannot be shipped because they require complex, pre-compiled
-    toolchains (node-vite and rust-rolldown) that are not yet packaged in
-    Debian and cannot be built offline.
-    The API and telemetry endpoints continue to work normally. Accessing the
-    root web endpoint will now display a static "No UI" placeholder page.
+  freshdeb: this is Prometheus 3, a major upgrade from the 2.x versions
+  the distributions ship.
 
- -- Reinhard Tartler <siretart@tauware.de>  Wed, 01 Jul 2026 03:57:00 -0400
+  Prometheus 3 reads the data Prometheus 2 wrote, and the default
+  configuration in /etc/prometheus/prometheus.yml works unchanged. Some
+  command-line flags, configuration settings and PromQL behaviours were
+  removed or changed, though: if you set flags in ARGS in
+  /etc/default/prometheus, changed the configuration or depend on
+  specific queries, check them against the migration guide:
+
+    https://prometheus.io/docs/prometheus/latest/migration/
+
+  Data written by Prometheus 3 can only be read by Prometheus 2.55 or
+  newer, so going back to the distribution's version afterwards isn't
+  possible.
+
+  Unlike Debian's own Prometheus 3 package, this one includes the web UI
+  (upstream's release build) and every service discovery mechanism.
+
+ -- freshdeb <packages@freshdeb.com>  Tue, 27 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
 
 prometheus (2.13.1+ds-1) unstable; urgency=medium
 
